{"study_accession":"PRJNA992805","secondary_study_accession":"SRP448204","title":"Zwitterionic Microgel Preservation Platform for Circulating Tumor Cells in Whole Blood Specimen","description":"The immediate processing of whole blood specimen is required in circulating tumor cell-based liquid biopsy. The reliable blood specimen stabilization toward preserving circulating tumor cells can enlarge the geographic sharing regions for precise rare-cell technology; however, it remains a challenge owing to circulating tumor cells fragility and rarity. Herein, we aim to establish a zwitterionic magnetic microgel platform to stabilize the whole blood specimen for long-term hypothermic preservation of model circulating tumor cells. In a cohort study of 20 cancer patients, their blood specimen can be preserved up to 7 days without compromising circulating tumor cell viability and RNA integrity, thereby excessively doubling the viable preservation duration. The 7day microgel-preserved blood specimen is able to reliably detect cancer-specific transcripts, similar to fresh blood specimens; while up/down expression regulation of 1243 genes in model circulating tumor cells preserved by commercial protectant. Mechanistically, the zwitterionic microgel assembly counters the cold-induced excessive reactive oxygen species and platelet activation, as well as extracellular matrix loss-induced cell anoikis, to prevent circulating tumor cell loss in the whole blood specimen. The present work serves as a springboard for the development of blood-based noninvasive diagnostics.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":15,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN36375159","study_accession":"PRJNA992805","blood_class":"whole_blood","class_from":"study","title":"Human sample from Homo sapiens","description":"replication 1","sex":"female","geo_sample":"","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2023-07-10","attributes":[["isolate","Fresh-1"],["age","0 day"],["biomaterial_provider","Meisen C